-- Version: 0.27.3
-- Description: Add work time tracking and WBS/Gantt attributes on service requests and activities, update work event object schemas and process procedures, seed AdminApp.Practices time_tracking.require_actual_on_close, seed adminCatalog:sections:manage_acl:all, seed AdminApp.Catalog allow.public.access, backfill missing catalog section read ACLs to registered, publish the HELP KB BPMN library article and the HELP KB events library article, add list to app.product_relation_kind, and require a null units_count on app.product_options unless relation_kind is required, and record how a process instance started and what a waiting token is waiting for, and replace the denormalized process procedure catalogs with the normalized procedure catalog.
-- Backend file: m_0.27.3_work_time_tracking.sql
--
-- Changes in v0.27.3:
-- - app.product_relation_kind adds list; app.product_options adds max_units_count INTEGER and updates product_options_units_count_check and chk_product_options_units for min/max required units.
-- - Add estimated_minutes and actual_minutes to app.service_requests, with non-negative checks.
-- - Add estimated_minutes, actual_minutes, and WBS/Gantt columns to app.activity_manual_tasks.
-- - Add WBS/Gantt columns to app.activity_approvals and app.activity_acceptances.
-- - Update work.manual_task, work.approval, and work.acceptance event object schemas (version 1) to match db/init/08_system_entities.sql.
-- - work.service_request.create/update and the manual activity create/update procedures keep the time and WBS/Gantt inputs inside the normalized app.process_procedures seed.
-- - Seed AdminApp.Practices time_tracking.require_actual_on_close. Conflict updates product-owned columns only and does not write value.
-- - Seed adminCatalog:sections:manage_acl:all and grant it to role.adminCatalog.admin, role.adminCatalog.editor, and sysadmins.
-- - Seed AdminApp.Catalog allow.public.access (boolean, default false, is_public true).
-- - Backfill a registered read ACL on catalog sections that do not already have one.
-- - app.users: idempotent chk_users_system_no_expires_at and the expires_at column comment (system accounts cannot set expires_at; NULL means no expiration).
-- - Publish the HELP KB BPMN library article (kba-sy1058) and link it from kba-sy1057.
-- - Publish the HELP KB events library article (kba-sy1059) from the event catalog seed.
-- - catalog.service_order.submitted summary says the order is for one of the services available in the catalog.
-- - app.process_instances and app.process_tokens gain the runtime columns, checks, comments, and indexes from db/init/05_tables.sql and db/init/06_indexes.sql. tgr_process_instances_guard_update freezes the start stamp.
-- - Drop app.process_system_procedures, app.process_manual_procedures, and app.process_external_procedures and seed app.process_procedure_namespaces, app.process_procedure_objects, and app.process_procedures from db/init/17_process_procedures.sql.

